---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'Finance for EOS and Vistage companies | Decisive';
const description =
  'The Scorecard tells you the boat is moving. We tell you if it is pointed at the money. Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days.';

const traps = [
  {
    name: 'Certainty Illusion',
    body: 'A Scorecard full of green can feel like proof the company is healthy. Some of those measurables stopped tracking money a while ago, and nobody is paid to notice. That is where the profit quietly leaks.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Mental Accounting',
    body: 'A Rock ships, the team celebrates, and a clean bottom line hides the product or client the rest of the business is quietly funding. The aggregate P&L keeps the secret. Full allocation gives it up.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Status Quo',
    body: 'A measurable nobody has re-baselined in three years is not stable. It is margin leaking at a rate nobody has priced, because the Scorecard row always looks the same.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">For EOS and Vistage operating companies</span>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">The Scorecard tells you the boat is moving.</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-line-accent">We tell you if it's pointed at the money.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        The Scorecard tracks activity. <span class="dollar">We track which of it makes money.</span> Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days. Typical 5x to 10x.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">30 minutes with Russ. No pitch. You leave knowing which measurables actually track the money.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">The empty seat</span>
        <h2>Your Scorecard measures motion. It doesn't measure profit.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          EOS gives you a Scorecard, Rocks, and an L10. What it assumes, and rarely names, is a Finance seat that can tell you which of those numbers actually makes money. Most operating companies run for years with that seat empty.
        </p>
        <div class="category-pull">
          Your books tell you what happened. They can't tell you what to do next.
        </div>
        <p>
          The decisions weren't wrong. You made them on the only numbers you had, and those numbers were never built to decide from. Everyone who touches your books is paid to serve something else: the filing, the close, the report. Nobody is paid to make the next call defensible, and that is the job we do.
        </p>
        <div class="delay-callout">
          We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="traps">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where the value is trapped</div>
      <h2>Three traps a green Scorecard hides.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);">
        The Six Trap Diagnostic&trade; reads your numbers through the decisions that produced them. Three of the six show up most often behind a healthy-looking Scorecard. The patterns are structural, not failures of the owner.
      </p>
      <div class="trap-grid">
        {traps.map((t, i) => (
          <div class="trap-card">
            <div class="trap-num">Trap {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="trap-name">{t.name}</div>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="traps-footer">
        We name the stack, price each one in dollars, and turn the read into a plan. We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Proof</span>
        <h2>An operating company that ran on data, and still wasn't getting the truth from it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="worked">
        <span class="label">Professional services, $30M revenue</span>
        <h4>A clean close is not a fast one, and neither tells you where the cash is stuck.</h4>
        <p>
          Cash was trapped in a billing and close cadence nobody had revisited, and clean-looking reports masked the leak. We rebuilt the rhythm, pulled the working capital forward, and put margin on a weekly line of sight.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Working capital recovered</span><span class="v accent">$380,000</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Close time</span><span class="v">22 to 3 days</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Margin improvement</span><span class="v">~$50,000 / mo</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 22px;">
        Anonymized by segment and revenue band until attribution is confirmed. The mechanism reads the same across industries because the traps do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Tiers and pricing</span>
        <h2>Find. Install. Run.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most owners start with the 14-day Decision Diagnostic and move into the 90-Day Resolution. Pricing is banded by revenue, and the floor is $5M.
        </p>
        <p class="promise-line">
          The Diagnostic promise: at least 3x the fee in owner-accepted value identified by Day 14, or you pay nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/#tiers">See tiers and pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guarantee">Read the guarantee</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Book a fit call</span>
      <h2>Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 14 days you know what your money is actually doing, in dollars: the traps that are running, the recoverable value, and the first three moves, whether or not we ever work together again. It starts with one 30-minute call.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-microcopy { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .promise-line { font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
